- The basic endpoints are simple and don't have obvious code injection vulnerabilities
- Uses Express properly with modular route handlers in this simple case

---

### Recommended Fixes for `app.js`:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const helmet = require('helmet');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');

const app = express();

// Security headers
app.use(helmet());

// Rate limiting
